    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hunters Estate Agent are delighted to present No.5 The Thicket, a beautifully refurbished detached bungalow, nestled in a quiet cul-de-sac off the tree lined Hainault Road. This elegant four-bedroom home offers 238sq.m. / 2,556sq.ft. of light filled accommodation, thoughtfully designed to balance aesthetic with everyday functionality.\r\n\r\nThe property was completely refurbished by the present owners in 2010 to an exacting standard, using quality materials and bespoke finishes. The reception rooms present picture windows overlooking the garden. The heart of the home, the kitchen/dining room incorporates a Newcastle Design kitchen and enjoys a sunny southwest orientation with French doors to the gardens. The main bedroom suite is complemented by a dressing room and shower room, and a generous family bathroom services the additional three bedrooms. There is an abundance of storage in the attic space, accessed via a Stira stairs.\r\n\r\nA striking feature of this very fine home is the prime corner position in the cul de sac and the private gardens. The front of the property is approached via a tarmacadam drive affording an abundance of off-street parking, bordered by mature high hedging and a lawn area with mature plants. The dual side access leads to the expansive southwest facing rear garden laid out with a generous patio area, specimen shrubs and herbaceous borders.\r\nIdeally located just a short stroll from the charming Foxrock village, residents enjoy easy access to boutique shops, eateries, and premier sporting facilities including Foxrock Golf Club, Leopardstown Racecourse, and Carrickmines Lawn Tennis Club. The area is well served by renowned schools and excellent transport links via the N11 (QBC), M50, and LUAS.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "ENTRANCE HALL\r\n8.23m x 2.16m (27'0\" x 7'1\")\r\nDecorative ceiling coving, recessed lighting and engineered oak floor. Cloaks and boots cupboard. Doors to the principal rooms.\r\n\r\nDRAWING ROOM\r\n8.02m x 4.64m (26'3\" x 15'2\")\r\nDual aspect room and a feature vaulted ceiling. Coal effect gas fire with a brass surround. Recessed lighting and engineered oak floor. Door to: -\r\n\r\nFAMILY ROOM/STUDY\r\n4.48m x 4.19m (14'8\" x 13'8\")\r\nVaulted ceiling with recessed lighting and engineered oak floor. Door to: -\r\n\r\nPLAYROOM\r\n4.87m x 3.22m (15'11\" x 10'6\")\r\nDecorative ceiling coving, recessed lighting and engineered oak floor. French door to the patio.\r\n\r\nKITCHEN/DINING ROOM\r\n7.32m x 4.87m (24'0\" x 15'11\")\r\nNewcastle designed kitchen with a silestone worktop incorporating a Belfast sink with under cabinet LED lights. Range of appliances to include a built-in Neff double oven, a Belling hob, and a Beko dishwasher and fridge. Decorative ceiling coving, recessed lighting and engineered oak floor. French doors to the gardens.\r\n\r\nUTILITY ROOM\r\n3.22m X 2.35m (10'6\" x 7'8\")\r\nGenerous storage space. Appliances to include a Hotpoint washing machine, Zanussi dryer, a Whirlpool fridge freezer and freezer. Decorative ceiling coving, recessed lighting and tiled floor.\r\n\r\nMAIN BEDROOM\r\n5.4m x 3.88m (17'8\" x 12'8\")\r\nDecorative ceiling coving, recessed lighting and engineered oak floor. Door to: -\r\n\r\nDRESSING ROOM\r\n5.67m x 2.35m (18'7\" x 7'8\")\r\nFloor to ceiling wardrobes and shelving. Decorative ceiling coving, recessed lighting and engineered oak floor. Hot-press with insulated cylinder.\r\n\r\nENSUITE\r\n2.43m x 1.38m (7'11\" x 4'6\")\r\nWhite suite incorporating a power shower unit, pedestal wash hand basin, wall mirror, medicine cabinet and wc. Recessed lighting and tiled walls and floors.\r\n\r\nFAMILY BATHROOM\r\n3.34m x 2.17m (10'11\" x 7'1\")\r\nWhite suite incorporating a free-standing bath, a power shower, pedestal wash hand basin, wall mirror, medicine cabinet and wc. Recessed lighting and tiled floor.\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 2\r\n3.44m x 3.35m (11'3\" x 10'11\")\r\nDecorative ceiling coving, recessed lighting and engineered oak floor. \r\n\r\nBEDROOM 3\r\n3.35m x 2.67m (10'11\" x 8'9\")\r\nRecessed lighting and engineered oak floor.\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 4\r\n4.41m x 2.9m (14'5\" x 9'6\")\r\nDual aspect room. Decorative ceiling coving, recessed lighting and engineered oak floor. \r\n\r\nOUTSIDE\r\nThe front of the property is approached via a tarmacadam drive affording an abundance of off-street parking, bordered by mature high hedging and a lawn area with mature plants. The dual side access leads to the expansive southwest facing rear garden laid out with a generous patio area, specimen shrubs and herbaceous borders. There is a large Seomra providing ample storage for sporting and garden equipment, and a wooden shed. There is external lighting, power points and an outdoor tap."
      },
      {
